{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtWvK55rig9THJj6CHNh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The system prompt is now split into two cached blocks, so a `save_fact` write only re-caches the per-athlete tail and the static coaching rules stay cached. I haven't confirmed this on the live API, and there's one risk you should check on the first real call.\n\n**What changed**\n- `bot.py`, `build_system()`: the static `INSTRUCTIONS` are now their own text block with a `cache_control` marker. The per-athlete context (date, profile, zones, goal, facts, language) is a second block with its own marker. Nothing in the first block is interpolated.\n- `README.md`: the caching paragraph describes the two blocks.\n- `ANSWER.md`: the cause, the change, verification, the open risk, and which parts of the colleague's note applied.\n\n**Verification:** I ran the bot with a fake LLM and temp data/log paths. Both blocks carry markers. The first block is identical before and after a `save_fact` write, and across a different athlete and date. The second block changes and contains the new fact. The real `data/athletes.json` and `logs/usage.jsonl` were not touched. I did not call the API; the sandbox has no key.\n\n**Risk to check:** Anthropic silently skips caching for a prefix below the model's minimum. The cached prefix is roughly the tool schemas plus instructions, and the log suggests it's close to the 1024-token minimum for `claude-sonnet-4-5`. If the first live call after deploy shows `cache_creation_input_tokens` at 0 for the instructions, the fix needs real content added to `INSTRUCTIONS`. I didn't pad it.\n\n**From the colleague's note:**\n- Applied: the two-block split with markers, a static first block with no interpolation, and only the tail re-cached after a memory write.\n- Not applied: relevance-based fact selection, which would change the tail on every message. I kept all facts.\n- Not fixed: tool-group changes still re-cache the whole prefix. The `plan_week` and `predict_race` rows in the log show this (~1300 tokens of cache creation). Avoiding it means sending the full tool set on every message, which is the cost the keyword filter was added to avoid. That's your call.\n\nI did not commit anything."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2201,"cache_read_input_tokens":40993,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2201},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"876677c9-22a0-45b4-b620-cf7440d648b6","uuid":"1124c2ad-b7d2-43e0-9b22-71e03bb71a8f","timestamp":"2026-11-10T03:12:36.427Z","request_id":"req_011CgtWvJuAKarEDAcvxRFfe"}
